  "model_id": "eleven_multilingual_v2",
  "text": "Sevilla score first. Their stadium explodes. And for a few minutes, it looks as if someone has finally interrupted Barcelona's perfect start. Then Raphinha appears between two defenders. One touch to shift the angle. One finish into the corner. By the end of the night he has three goals, Barcelona have three points, and the question is bigger than another hat-trick. How do you defend a player who is no longer where the old scouting report says he should be? The goals are spectacular. The movement behind them is the real problem. And across Europe, that distinction is about to matter."
